latest_quarter.body:
- **Q1 FY27 (this):** First note for GSMFOILS — identity established. Revenue INR96.9cr (+86.3% YoY), EBITDA
  INR11.5cr (11.9%, +70bps), PAT INR7.6cr (7.9%, +80bps). Ahmedabad at 35% utilisation. Unit 3 (ROPP caps,
  MOU with AAPL Solutions) began commercial production June 2026 with first billing ~19-Jul-2026. Unit 4
  (export foil, Sarigam/Vapi plant relocating to Vasai) announced as imminent but **not yet formally
  confirmed** on the call. Promoter Shri Mohan Singh Parmar sold 12% in Q1; voluntary 1.5-year lock-in
  followed. INR40–50cr bank debt under negotiation, unsanctioned. FY27 guide INR450–500cr (also stated as
  INR400–450cr) with ~INR35cr PAT and ~12% EBITDA margin held through Q2/Q3; FY28 guide INR750–800cr.
- _Q2 FY27 → check:_ (1) **did Unit 4 start production by end-August 2026** and was the Sarigam deal signed;
  (2) **was the INR40–50cr facility sanctioned** (he said "a month or two" from 21-Jul-2026);
  (3) Ahmedabad utilisation vs the 35% → >80% path — is it tracking to ~INR30cr/month by Q4;
  (4) did the **12% EBITDA margin hold** as promised for Q2, with aluminium now falling;
  (5) ROPP revenue vs the INR30–35cr FY27 path, and whether the 18–20% takeaway margin is confirmed with
  actual numbers rather than industry hearsay;
  (6) receivable days vs the stated 75–80 range, and whether OCF is still negative;
  (7) **which FY27 revenue number management repeats** — INR450–500cr or INR400–450cr;
  (8) whether directors' remuneration is charged in Q2 (Q1 carried none);
  (9) first export shipment via the merchant exporter, and any move toward direct exporting.

